CHAPTER III

FORMS OF VIOLENCE AGAINST

WOMEN AND CHILDREN

Article 4

Forms of violence against women and children include:

a. physical violence;

b. psychological violence;

c. sexual violence;

d. neglect;

e. exploitation; and/or

f. other violence.

Article 7

1. Sexual violence as referred to in Article 4 letter c includes:
a. non-physical sexual harassment;
b. physical sexual harassment;
c. forced contraception;
d. forced sterilization;
e. forced marriage;
f. sexual torture;
g. sexual exploitation;
h. sexual slavery; and
i. electronic-based sexual violence
2. In addition to Sexual Violence Crimes as referred to in paragraph (1), Sexual Violence Crimes also include:
a. rape;
b. indecent acts;
c. intercourse with Children, indecent acts against Children, and/or sexual exploitation of Children;
d. acts violating decency that are contrary to the victim's will and religious values recognized in Indonesia;
e. pornography involving Children or pornography that explicitly contains violence and sexual exploitation;
f. forced prostitution;
g. criminal acts of trafficking in persons intended for sexual exploitation;
h. sexual violence within the domestic sphere;
i. criminal acts of money laundering where the predicate offense constitutes a Sexual Violence Crime; and
j. other criminal acts expressly stated as Sexual Violence Crimes as regulated in the provisions of laws and regulations.

