Article 17

1. To prevent acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government conducts empowerment and builds awareness among families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.
2. In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government undertakes efforts as follows:
a. providing material on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in formal, non-formal, and informal education;
b. providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;

